LAWS REQUIRED: associative, identity
   ℕ under ×
     associative: True
     identity:    True   it is 1
     inverses:    False   none for 0, 2, 3
     commutative: True
   ℕ under gcd
     associative: True
     identity:    True   it is 0
     inverses:    False   none for 1, 2, 3
     commutative: True
   strings under concatenation (sample)
     associative: True
     identity:    True   it is ''
     inverses:    False   none for 'a', 'b', 'ab'
     commutative: False   fails at 'a', 'b'
   subsets of {1, 2} under ∪
     associative: True
     identity:    True   it is ∅
     inverses:    False   none for {1}, {2}, {1, 2}
     commutative: True
   positive integers 1..6 under + (the non-example)
     associative: True
     identity:    False   none in the sample
     inverses:    False
     commutative: True
   each monoid has exactly one identity, and it is the value of an empty chain:
   sum([]) = 0, math.prod([]) = 1, ''.join([]) = ''
